//? Title: Point model checks:complete graphs on genuine CAD surfaces
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Original ModelNet surfaces feed complete PointNet and PointNet++graphs. Every endpoint/gradient,identity T-Net,orthogonality penalty and ordering check is explicit,with independent source-sampling and derivative oracles.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/point_models_checks.cpp`.

> The method

Keep every source T-Net/shared MLP or set abstraction,execute full and compact graphs on original CAD surfaces,and distinguish frozen discrete grouping from differentiable point features. These initialization checks fit no classifier;training remains explicit in the following model reports.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/point_models_checks_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/point_models_checks_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/point_models_checks_concept.tikz > build/point_models_checks_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/point_models_checks_concept.svg build/point_models_checks_concept.dvi > build/point_models_checks_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
