> Verification and scope

Six native tests execute original nine-entry penalty derivatives,both full
and compact graph inventories,every finite derivative on genuine1024point
surfaces,identity/permutation checks,an independent all18coordinate shared
MLP/population-BN/input finite-difference fixture,every compact source row,
all moving-state modes and invalid inputs. Fourteen public examples compile
and run. The original complete checks and independent mesh sampling replay
pass. These are supporting architecture checks;the following two reports
show actual explicit optimizer loops and every held-out classification error.

> Conclusion

Complete graphs and independent numerical/source-data checks pass. PointNet logits retain permutation invariance within tolerance,while the source PointNet++grouping remains order dependent. Initialized features and penalties establish implementation contracts without a classification-quality claim.

> References

- [Qi et al.(2017),PointNet:Deep Learning on Point Sets for3DClassification and Segmentation](https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.00593).
- [Qi et al.(2017),PointNet++:Deep Hierarchical Feature Learning on Point Sets in a Metric Space](https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.02413).
- [Original Princeton ModelNet data](https://modelnet.cs.princeton.edu/).
